### Personal Financial Tracker API — manual request collection
### Requires the "REST Client" extension (VS Code/Cursor) or a JetBrains IDE's
### built-in HTTP client. Run `npm run dev` first, then click "Send Request"
### above any request below. New endpoints should get a request here as they
### land, so this file stays a live, runnable map of the API surface.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Health check — confirms the server is up
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Auth: current session (expect 200 + null body when logged out)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/get-session

### Auth: register via Better Auth's own endpoint (autoSignIn: false — no session is created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manual-test@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123",
  "name": "Manual Test"
}

### Auth: same email again — should return the same 200 shape (enumeration protection).
### Check the DB directly (see docs/DECISIONS.md) to confirm no second row was created.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manual-test@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123",
  "name": "Manual Test"
}

### Sanity check: a genuinely unmounted path should still 404 (mount is scoped, not catch-all)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/totally-made-up-path

### Auth: sign-in (wrong password on purpose). Click "Send Request" 6x within
### 60s — the first 5 should return 401, the 6th should return 429
### (customRules rate limit on /sign-in/email, see docs/DECISIONS.md).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ratelimit-test@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword123"
}

### Auth: make sure the test user exists before signing in — safe to
### re-run any time (duplicate sign-up returns the same 200 shape, see the
### enumeration-protection request above). Needed again any time
### manual-test@example.com's auth_user row gets deleted by hand, e.g.
### while cleaning up orphaned rows predating the onUserCreate hook.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manual-test@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123",
  "name": "Manual Test"
}

### Auth: sign-in with correct credentials — expect 200 + Set-Cookie
### (better-auth.session_token, HttpOnly; see issue #9 and docs/DECISIONS.md
### — "Логін напряму через /api/auth/sign-in/email, без кастомної обгортки").
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manual-test@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123"
}

### Auth: confirm the session cookie from the request above actually works.
### REST Client / JetBrains HTTP client keep cookies per file, so sending
### this right after should return the session, not null.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/get-session

### Accounts: create (requires the session cookie from sign-in above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Main Card",
  "type": "card",
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Accounts: list all accounts belonging to the authenticated user
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts

### Accounts: get one by id — replace with a real id from the create response above
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Accounts: update — replace with a real id
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/accounts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Renamed Card"
}

### Accounts: delete — replace with a real id (expect 204, no body)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/e691a354-7e82-4e01-9baf-6c96e0119cb5
